X:1
T:Jackarse Eat It On The Way
% NFF Book 2006
S:collected from George Blackman, Mudgee, NSW
S:John Meredith Collection, NLA
B:J Meredith, R Covell, & P Brown, Folk Songs of Australia Vol 2, UNSW Press, 1987, p296
Z:arranged by Greg O'Leary
N:This is a version of "Spanish Ladies", but with the parts reversed and a
N:syncopation in the A part, probably due to an accordion taking the easy way
N:out. The tune's phrases mostly end on a minor chord, which is the result of
N:only one note being changed, but radically alters the sound. This transforms
N:a pleasant melody into a very strong fiddle tune. Greg O'Leary, 2007
O:Australia, NSW, Mudgee
R:Set Tune
